  "verbalization": "Acanthosessilioside C is shown to have a target relationship with Jurkat, a cell line that is known to be targeted by this compound. Jurkat is further identified as a target of multiple complex molecular entities, including a long-chain fatty acid derivative and a spirocyclic compound. All these molecular entities are linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, a key enzyme involved in drug metabolism and detoxification. The evidence suggests that Acanthosessilioside C may act through a mechanism that involves targeting Jurkat, which in turn interacts with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The shared involvement of Jurkat and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 implies a potential pathway where Acanthosessilioside C may influence the enzyme's activity or regulation. The evidence is consistent across multiple molecular entities, suggesting a broader functional relationship that may involve the enzyme in the metabolic processing of these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the enzyme's role in the metabolic fate of the drug targets, reinforcing the possibility of a direct or indirect interaction between Acanthosessilioside C and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4.",
